<title>GERMANY: Duisenberg-EMU stability pact &quot;just around corner&quot;.</title>
<headline>Duisenberg-EMU stability pact &quot;just around corner&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch central bank governor Wim Duisenberg said on Friday he was pleased that a stability pact to enforce discipline on members of the planned single European currency was &quot;just around the corner&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;I am very pleased indeed, from what I hear from Dublin, that a stability pact is just around the corner,&quot; Duisenberg told journalists at a briefing at the European Monetary Institute in Frankfurt to unveil the new euro currency.</p>
<p>Duisenberg also said he did not expect a delay in the start of currency union.</p>
<p>Duisenberg is scheduled to take over leadership of the Frankfurt-based EMI, which is the forerunner to the European central bank. The European central bank comes into being after currency union, which is slated to begin in January 1999 as outlined in the Maastricht Treaty.</p>
<p>--Catherine O'Mahony, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 6 9756525</p>
